title: '[pallet-revive] Deletion queue keeps the native deposit records of a re-created contract'

doc:
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    A contract created at the address of a terminated contract, for example with `CREATE2` and
    the same deployer, code and salt, keeps its per-payer native deposit records while the
    deletion queue is still removing the storage of the terminated contract. Before, the
    deletion queue could clear those records, and a payer who later freed storage in the new
    contract did not get the native deposit back. This happened when the terminated contract
    had no native deposit records, or when removing its storage took more than one batch.

- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    No migration, configuration change or runtime action is needed.

    `ContractInfo::process_deletion_queue_batch` now clears the `NativeDepositOf` rows of a
    queued contract only while no contract is live at its address. The child trie of the
    terminated contract is removed as before.

    The per-entry deletion-queue weight (`WeightInfo::deletion_queue_per_entry`) now includes
    one `AccountInfoOf` read. Runtimes should regenerate their `pallet_revive` weights.

    The `MultiContributorStorage` fixture gains a `clearStorage` function, which adds a variant
    to the generated `MultiContributorStorage::MultiContributorStorageCalls` enum in
    `pallet-revive-fixtures`.

crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: major
